During our discussions, Lottie and I have identified a number of different identities, masks or classifications of bahaviour.
These classifactions were more than just amusing anecodtes, they were essential to explaining to Lottie how my personality worked.
They were also intensely helpful to me personally to understand myself better as I grapple with how influential, inextiricable and imporant my ADHD has influenced the person I became, in both its wonderous and terrible forms.
In other words, this set of identities helps elucidate the ways I interact with the world. 

This will take the form of individual entries in this part of the archive for each of those identities as we go through and analyse our previous discussions about these topics.
These individual entries will be expanded upon in future discussion as we grow to understand them better.

Here is a first presentation of this list as they exist at the present moment:
[1] Nemesis the avenging angel: the one who descends to protect me at times when my identity as an artist is questioned - unforgiving, relentless and forthright, the angenging angel takes no prisoners and will defend my right to be myself no matter the cost to my own or anyone else's sanity.
[2] Wilting Petal, the aggrieved: ever the victim, the wllting petal believes he deserves exactly what he had coming;
[3] Captain Wise, the obtuse: steps in and demands what is not his due to ignorance
[4] Evil Twin, the nefarious: faces reality with a wicked smile - pretends to be nefarious but dus so witha grin.
[5] Prof. Ekeleiburg, the coldly distant: the cosmic trickster who is aloof of reality and concerned with the esoteric and the occult.
[6] Slaggy Tramp, the unabashed: who will keep on dancing no matter what - exuberant and sensual to a tee, you can always rely on the slaggy tramp to demand fulfillment of bodily desires and the senses.
[7] Mucky Angel, the optimistic: who will tread where no normal angel would dare because he is oblivious danger - he stares not at the stars thus not seeing the dogshit.
[8] Gänan, the negator and annihilator: the one most deeply buried in the little green box - who rears his ugly head in fits of rage and who intends to bring everyone, including myself, down with him - he fears no slippage because he is already there.

Note that we also used the term "the real me" to define another identity. Here's the thing: they are ALL the real me. All at once. It's just that one of them gets the upperhand and they generally balance each other out. This is a separate category is therefore pointless.
